      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A diabetic patient with renal insufficiency and a giant ventricular aneurysm was treated by continuous ambulatory peritoneal dialysis (CAPD). No apparent exacerbation of the patient's cardiovascular function was observed after starting CAPD therapy, although his ejection fraction remained low and his angina attacks persisted. It is suggested that CAPD therapy has no deleterious effects on the cardiovascular system of patients with ventricular aneurysms, and that the benefits outweigh the risks."},
